  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Information Technology reported $252M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. General Dynamics Information Technology won 82 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $3.1M. General Dynamics Information Technology obligations are down 94.9% year over year versus the prior full fiscal year. General Dynamics Information Technology annual obligations ranged from $4.1B in FY22 to $4.9B in FY26, and then $252M in FY27 to date. General Dynamics Information Technology concentration in FY2027 to date is highest in Computer Systems Design Services with $123M, followed by Other Computer Related Services with $60.5M and Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds with $38.3M. General Dynamics Information Technology received the largest buying-agency obligations from the Department of Health and Human Services with $62.9M and the Department of Commerce with $61M, while the Department of Justice and the Department of State show $0 in obligations in FY2027 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is General Dynamics Information Technology's FY2027 to date business?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Information Technology shows heavy concentration in a few NAICS markets: Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $123M and Other Computer Related Services accounts for $60.5M. General Dynamics Information Technology also has meaningful activity in Pharmacy Benefit Management and Other Third Party Administration of Insurance and Pension Funds at $38.3M. General Dynamics Information Technology has limited obligations in lower-tier markets, including Environmental Consulting Services at $438K and Marketing Consulting Services at $200K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are driving General Dynamics Information Technology's FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Information Technology obligations are led by the Department of Health and Human Services at $62.9M and the Department of Commerce at $61M. General Dynamics Information Technology also received obligations from the Department of the Interior at $33.7M and the Department of Transportation at $30.8M. General Dynamics Information Technology has $0 in obligations from the Department of Justice and $0 from the Department of State in FY2027 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
